WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.598
Welcome to Grade 6 English, Unit 6: People and Work.

2
00:00:03.678 --> 00:00:06.782
In this unit the focus is on people and work.

3
00:00:06.862 --> 00:00:12.936
You will explore the many different jobs and
professions that keep communities running,

4
00:00:13.016 --> 00:00:17.251
from physicians and lawyers to food vendors and commentators.

5
00:00:17.331 --> 00:00:23.123
You will learn how people choose their
careers, what skills different jobs require,

6
00:00:23.203 --> 00:00:29.843
and how the world of work connects to ideas of
fairness, justice, and community responsibility.

7
00:00:29.923 --> 00:00:35.785
In this short lecture, preview the key
ideas and prepare for the independent lesson.

8
00:00:35.865 --> 00:00:43.611
By the end of this unit, you will be able to identify
and describe a range of professions and career paths,

9
00:00:43.691 --> 00:00:47.487
explaining the skills and training each one requires.

10
00:00:47.567 --> 00:00:53.630
You will also explain how personal interests
and strengths can guide career choices.

11
00:00:53.710 --> 00:01:02.113
You will also read a passage about careers and jobs and
answer comprehension questions at different thinking levels.

12
00:01:02.193 --> 00:01:04.819
Keep these goals in mind as you work.

13
00:01:04.899 --> 00:01:11.332
Your vocabulary work begins with these words: wisdom,
script, text, commentary, observation, caption.

14
00:01:11.412 --> 00:01:16.555
Listen to each pronunciation in the
vocabulary lab, study its meaning in context,

15
00:01:16.635 --> 00:01:20.617
and use the word accurately in
your own discussion and writing.

16
00:01:20.697 --> 00:01:27.025
The reading sequence includes The People Who Keep
a Community Running and Four Professions, One Town.

17
00:01:27.105 --> 00:01:27.913
Read actively.

18
00:01:27.993 --> 00:01:32.291
Identify each text's central ideas,
notice viewpoint and reliability,

19
00:01:32.371 --> 00:01:36.415
and support every inference with
relevant evidence from the text.

20
00:01:36.495 --> 00:01:41.767
The first language focus is Compound
Nouns: Closed, Hyphenated and Open Forms.

21
00:01:41.847 --> 00:01:47.874
A compound noun joins two or more words to
make one noun with a single, specific meaning,

22
00:01:47.954 --> 00:01:51.991
and English writes these compounds in three different forms.

23
00:01:52.071 --> 00:01:59.471
Notice the structure in the model examples, then apply
it deliberately in connected sentences and paragraphs.

24
00:01:59.551 --> 00:02:04.060
In speaking, you will complete
Speaking 1: Career Interview Role-Play.

25
00:02:04.140 --> 00:02:08.452
Organise your ideas, use evidence
and respond clearly to questions.

26
00:02:08.532 --> 00:02:11.795
In writing, you will plan, draft, check and revise.

27
00:02:11.875 --> 00:02:15.269
Use the success criteria before submitting your work.

28
00:02:15.349 --> 00:02:16.969
You are ready to begin.

29
00:02:17.049 --> 00:02:24.288
Start with the vocabulary lab, continue through
reading and comprehension, apply the grammar focus,

30
00:02:24.368 --> 00:02:27.837
and complete the speaking and writing practices.

31
00:02:27.917 --> 00:02:36.190
Use the AI tutor for hints and feedback any time, and
bring your questions to a live session too if you join one.
